<%# The three stages an overdue member moves through, in one place. Admins kept reading the
    past-due reminder and the lapse notice as two unrelated mailings going to two unrelated
    groups; they are consecutive, and the counts below are the same people at different
    points in the sequence. %>
<div class="card shadow-sm border-0 mb-3">
  <div class="card-body py-3">
    <div class="h-section-label mb-2">What an overdue member hears, in order</div>
    <div class="table-responsive">
      <table class="table table-compact mb-0">
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th>When</th>
            <th>Email</th>
            <th>Who is there now</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <td class="text-nowrap">Dues date, for <%= pluralize(@reminder_setting.start_offset_days, 'day') %></td>
            <td class="text-secondary">Nothing — waiting out the start offset</td>
            <td>
              <% if @payment_overdue_grace_count.to_i.positive? %>
                <span class="fw-medium"><%= @payment_overdue_grace_count %></span> waiting
              <% else %>
                <span class="text-secondary">Nobody waiting</span>
              <% end %>
            </td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td class="text-nowrap">
              Until <%= @membership_setting.overdue_grace_period_days %> days overdue
            </td>
            <td>
              <% if @payment_overdue_email_template %>
                <%= link_to @payment_overdue_email_template.name, email_template_path(@payment_overdue_email_template),
                            class: "text-decoration-none" %>
              <% else %>
                Payment Past Due
              <% end %>
              <span class="text-secondary">· repeats every <%= pluralize(@reminder_setting.interval_days, 'day') %><%= ", up to #{@reminder_setting.max_reminders}" unless @reminder_setting.unlimited_reminders? %></span>
            </td>
            <td>
              <% if @payment_overdue_reminded_count.to_i.positive? %>
                <span class="fw-medium"><%= @payment_overdue_reminded_count %></span> being reminded
              <% else %>
                <span class="text-secondary">Nobody being reminded</span>
              <% end %>
              <span class="text-secondary">· <%= @payment_overdue_due_count %> due on the next run</span>
            </td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td class="text-nowrap">
              At <%= @membership_setting.overdue_grace_period_days %> days overdue
            </td>
            <td>
              <% if @membership_lapsed_email_template %>
                <%= link_to @membership_lapsed_email_template.name, email_template_path(@membership_lapsed_email_template),
                            class: "text-decoration-none" %>
              <% else %>
                Membership Lapsed
              <% end %>
              <span class="text-secondary">· once, as they fall inactive</span>
            </td>
            <td class="text-secondary">Anyone still unpaid when their grace runs out</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <div class="text-12 text-secondary mt-2">
      Every stage counts from the dues date, including the two in
      <%= link_to "Membership settings", membership_settings_path, class: "text-secondary" %>: a member's standing reads
      Current for the payment grace period, <%= pluralize(@membership_setting.payment_grace_period_days, 'day') %> while
      their payment could still be clearing, and Overdue from then until they lapse.
      All three stages are governed by the Enabled switch on the reminders page, and a member who opts out opts out of
      the whole sequence. The lapse notice fires on the move to inactive rather than on the daily run, so “Send now”
      covers the past-due reminders only.
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
